{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3404","published":"2026-08-20T09:54:29Z","modified":"2026-08-20T10:15:06.354743528Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-8177"],"summary":"perl-XML-LibXML security update","details":"This module is Perl Binding for libxml2, which implements a Perl interface to the GNOME libxml2 library. This module provides interfaces for parsing and manipulating XML files and allows Perl programmers to use the highly capable validating XML parser and the high performance DOM implementation.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nXML::LibXML versions through 2.0210 for Perl read out-of-bounds heap memory when parsing XML node names containing truncated UTF-8 byte sequences.\n\nA node name ending in the middle of a multi byte UTF-8 sequence causes the parser to read past the end of the input string into adjacent heap memory.\n\nAny Perl process that passes attacker controlled strings to XML::LibXML&apos;s DOM node-name methods can reach this path on the default API. The likely consequence is a crash, causing denial of service.(CVE-2026-8177)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"perl-XML-LibXML","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/perl-XML-LibXML&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.0134-2.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["perl-XML-LibXML-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","perl-XML-LibXML-debuginfo-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","perl-XML-LibXML-debugsource-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","perl-XML-LibXML-help-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["perl-XML-LibXML-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["perl-XML-LibXML-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","perl-XML-LibXML-debuginfo-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","perl-XML-LibXML-debugsource-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","perl-XML-LibXML-help-2.0134-2.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-3404.json"}},{"package":{"name":"perl-XML-LibXML","ecosystem